#GALE (erf-model/GALE)
    -- ERF is a git submodule (Submodules/ERF); GALE holds only its own files, its CTest
       suite (Tests/, Turbines/Tests) and its documentation site (Docs/sphinx_doc,
       https://erf-model.github.io/GALE/). ERF's release history is in Submodules/ERF/CHANGES.

#ERF-MovingBodies 26.10 (standalone branch, hgopalan/ERF #449-#468)
    -- Moving-bodies actuator framework: velocity sampling and force spreading on
       uniform, stretched and terrain-fitted meshes; anchor level on multi-level grids

    -- OpenFAST turbine coupling (FAST_Library, ExtInfw): lockstep stepping, restart,
       start-up audit; actuator disk (plain, upstream and corrected sampling) and
       actuator line with the filtered lifting-line correction; tower and nacelle forces

    -- Prescribed-Ct disks, farms, wake lines, running statistics, turbulent inflow
       from precursor planes or cell perturbations, bodies on terrain

    -- Canonical cases with golds, box-parity and restart-parity tests, OpenFAST-stub CI job

    -- Audit of the whole area: the corrected disk's free-stream update is under-relaxed
       from its loop gain and held to a time scale by default (correction_relax,
       correction_time); restart
       checks (same bodies and inputs, step, OpenFAST stop time) and log trimming; runs
       that stop at stop_datetime; finer levels over the bodies abort; input checks
       (finite values, ranges, unused keys); start-up abort and restart-abort tests
